  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USING HEALTHCARE AND CONSERVATION INCENTIVES TO PROTECT ORANGUTAN HABITAT IN INDONESIAN BORNEO -- CYCLE 12: RESTORING RAINFOREST ECOSYSTEMS AND SUPPORTING SUSTAINABLE ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PRIMARY GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CONSERVE AND RESTORE BORNEAN ORANGUTAN HABITAT IN WEST KALIMANTAN THROUGH HEALTHCARE AND CONSERVATION INCENTIVES, REFORESTATION, AND SUPPORTING A JUST TRANSITION FROM LOGGING TO SUSTAINABLE ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS. PROJECT OBJECTIVES INCLUDE, (1) EXPAND REGENERATIVE FARMING TRAINING OPPORTUNITIES AND INCREASE SUPPORT FOR ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS FOR FORMER LOGGERS (2) PROVIDE HIGH-QUALITY, AFFORDABLE HEALTHCARE AS AN INCENTIVE TO PROTECT ORANGUTAN HABITAT (3) RESTORE 72 HECTARES OF ORANGUTAN HABITAT THROUGH REFORESTATION AND (4) INCREASE BIODIVERSITY MONITORING TO IDENTIFY AND PROTECT CRITICAL ORANGUTAN HABITAT.</narrative>
  </description>
